CODEX_INSTRUCTIONS.md: DiscStats - Form & Metric AnalyzerProject OverviewDiscStats is an open-source, zero-cost web application for disc golfers to analyze throw biomechanics and flight metrics from side-view videos. Using client-side computer vision (WebAssembly), DiscStats extracts hand speed, body momentum, release angles, hyzer angle, and spin rate (for multi-color/split discs) without requiring dedicated backend hardware or cloud GPU costs.Technical Stack & ConstraintsInfrastructure & Hosting ($0 Cost Boundary)Deployment & Hosting: Vercel (Hobby Free Tier).Framework: Next.js (App Router, TypeScript, React 19).Database, Auth & Storage: Supabase Free Tier (PostgreSQL, GoTrue Auth, Storage bucket for low-res thumbnails only).Styling & UI: Tailwind CSS, Shadcn/UI, Lucide React icons.Data Visualization: Recharts (for analytics trends, consistency radar, and 2D flight path preview).Vision & Processing EngineEngine: Client-side execution using @mediapipe/tasks-vision (Pose Landmarker running in WebAssembly via Web Workers).Processing Boundary: Zero server-side video uploads or GPU server instances. All video processing occurs inside the browser's HTML5 Canvas and Web Worker pipeline.Project Structure & Architecture BlueprintPlaintext├── app/
